# Dependencies
node_modules
npm-debug.log
# package-lock.json is deliberately NOT ignored. Excluding it meant `COPY
# package*.json ./` never copied it, so the Dockerfile's `[ -f
# package-lock.json ]` test failed and every build silently fell through to
# `npm install`, resolving fresh versions from the registry at build time. Two
# images built from the same commit could therefore ship different dependency
# trees, with nothing in the repo recording the difference.

